1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:03,500
Ladies and gentlemen,

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,800
Amtrak is happy to announce our arrival in New York City.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,100
The train will be stopping in five minutes.

4
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:08,300
Please check to be sure you have your belongings.

5
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,800
And have a good stay in the Big Apple.

6
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:11,855
Thank you.

7
00:00:11,855 --> 00:00:13,700
Well, here we are.

8
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:16,500
It was so nice meeting you, Mr.Stewart.

9
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,800
And nice meeting you, too, Mrs.Tobin.

10
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,300
Please look us up.

11
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:22,500
We're in the phone book.

12
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,800
Dr. Philip Stewart, in Riverdale.

13
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:26,900
Your son?

14
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:31,100
That's right. And have a good time in New York.

15
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:33,600
And don't be so independent.

16
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:49,700
You're very lucky to have a caring family.

17
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:50,600
When can we go fishing?

18
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,300
Robbie, we'll go fishing soon,

19
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,000
and we'll take your dad with us.

20
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,400
I'm ready, Grandpa. You name the day.

21
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,600
That's a great idea, Grandpa!

22
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,700
Philip needs a day off.

23
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:06,000
Let's give him our presents--now.

24
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:06,900
Good idea.

25
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:12,540
Presents--for me?

26
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:14,500
From me and Marilyn.

27
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,800
And this one's from me.

28
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:34,758
I looked all over the house to find it.

29
00:01:34,758 --> 00:01:45,300
Richard, these are terrific pictures.

30
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:50,181
This one really brings back memories.

31
00:01:50,181 --> 00:01:51,703
You remember that day, Robbie?

32
00:01:51,703 --> 00:01:58,001
I sure do. It was fun.

33
00:01:58,001 --> 00:02:05,500
Oh, I'm sorry Susan isn't here.

34
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,100
I miss her very much.

35
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:10,300
She feels bad, too, Grandpa.

36
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:12,600
She called to say the plane was delayed.

37
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:14,100
You know airports.

38
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:16,857
I can't wait to see her.

39
00:02:16,857 --> 00:02:22,767
She looks just like Grandma at that age.

40
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:24,727
I'd better unpack.

41
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:31,364
I started traveling twenty-four hours ago.

42
00:02:31,364 --> 00:02:34,816
I'm not so young anymore.

43
00:02:34,816 --> 00:02:36,379
Don't you want something to eat?

44
00:02:36,379 --> 00:02:38,900
No, thanks.

45
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:41,800
After a good night's sleep, I'll enjoy breakfast even more.

46
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,900
Well, come on, Dad.

47
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,800
Ellen and I'll take you to your room.

48
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:47,700
I'm sure glad you're here, Grandpa.

49
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:48,289
Good night, Grandpa.

50
00:02:48,289 --> 00:03:04,895
Pleasant dreams.

51
00:03:04,895 --> 00:03:09,000
Philip, do you have the key to the trunk?

52
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:17,751
I have the key, but it doesn't work.

53
00:03:17,751 --> 00:03:32,138
I sent the wrong key.

54
00:03:32,138 --> 00:03:38,200
I have something for you. I made it myself.

55
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:41,500
I think you'll enjoy it.

56
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:44,200
I researched it for over a year.

57
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:49,949
It's our family tree.

58
00:03:49,949 --> 00:03:53,900
Oh, Grandpa! How exciting!

59
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:55,500
Fabulous!

60
00:03:55,500 --> 00:04:00,300
Why, I didn't know that your grandfather was born in Germany.

61
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:04,000
Lots of interesting information about our family.

62
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,834
A gift from me.

63
00:04:06,834 --> 00:04:09,332
Thank you so much.

64
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:11,471
Grandpa! Grandpa!

65
00:04:11,471 --> 00:04:15,600
Oh, Grandpa, I'm so happy to see you!

66
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:22,000
Oh, you look so beautiful, Susan. My granddaughter.

67
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:27,600
Like I always said, you look just like Grandma.

68
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:31,300
I think you're going to be very happy here with us.

69
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:34,157
I know you will.

70
00:04:34,157 --> 00:04:37,157
I don't feel alone anymore.
